<footer class="kh-footer kh-u-fullbleed kh-u-do-not-print kh-content" role="contentinfo">
  {#- The bio appears once per page, never twice. The homepage says it in the
      hero; entries say it in the byline at the foot of the piece, which is
      where a reader who has just finished reading actually asks the question.
      Everything else -- indexes, topics, stats, search, utility pages -- has
      no other statement of identity, so the footer carries it there.
      Keep this condition in step with the layouts that include
      partials/author-note.njk. -#}
  {%- set hasByline = layout in ["layouts/post.njk", "layouts/digesting.njk"] -%}
  {%- if page.url != "/" and not hasByline %}
  {%- markdown %}
  <strong>I'm Ken Hawkins</strong>. I lead digital platforms and audience engagement, building public-facing systems that help complex organizations reach, serve, and learn from their audiences. I structure their content and data to be usable by people and the machines increasingly reading on their behalf. <a href="/">Learn more</a> or <a href="/#hello">get in touch</a>.
  {% endmarkdown -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {#- Grouped, not a single row. This was six links of five different kinds on
      one line -- legal, meta, primary content, a profile, a subscribe action
      and a UI control -- with no relationship expressed between them. "Work"
      in particular is primary content and was sitting between GitHub and
      Colophon as though it were an afterthought.

      Columns use the mono micro-label from the datasheet register, so the
      footer reads as deliberate structure rather than a leftover list. -#}
  <nav class="kh-footer__nav" aria-label="Site">
    <div class="kh-footer__group">
      <p class="kh-meta kh-footer__label">Writing</p>
      <ul class="kh-footer__list">
        <li><a href="/blog">Blog</a></li>
        <li><a href="/digesting">Digesting</a></li>
        <li><a href="/work">Work</a></li>
        <li><a href="/topics/">Topics</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="kh-footer__group">
      <p class="kh-meta kh-footer__label">This site</p>
      <ul class="kh-footer__list">
        <li><a href="/all/">All writing</a></li>
        <li><a href="/search/">Search</a></li>
        <li><a href="/stats/">Stats</a></li>
        <li><a href="/colophon">Colophon</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="kh-footer__group">
      <p class="kh-meta kh-footer__label">Elsewhere</p>
      <ul class="kh-footer__list">
        <li><a href="https://github.com/khawkins98" rel="me">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://toot.io/@khawkins98" rel="me">Mastodon</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/allaboutken">LinkedIn</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="kh-footer__group">
      <p class="kh-meta kh-footer__label">Small print</p>
      <ul class="kh-footer__list">
        <li><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a></li>
        <li><a href="/impressum">Impressum</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </nav>

  {#- Two controls rather than two links, so they sit apart from the nav.
      The CSS toggle is the most distinctive thing on the site and used to be
      the sixth item in a flat list; it is a feature, not a destination.
      NOTE: #kh-css-toggle must stay in the DOM -- every style on the site is
      scoped to `body:has(#kh-css-toggle:checked)`. -#}
  <div class="kh-footer__controls">
    <span class="kh-footer__control">
      <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>
      <span class="kh-meta">Instant updates with the hottest tech from 20 years ago</span>
    </span>
    <label class="kh-footer__control kh-u-text--nowrap" title="Toggle site CSS on or off">
      <input type="checkbox" id="kh-css-toggle" name="css-toggle" checked>
      CSS
      <span class="kh-meta">Turn the design off</span>
    </label>
  </div>

  {%- if serverInfo.environment == "development" %}
      <div class="kh-banner kh-banner--alert kh-banner--warning">
        <p class="kh-banner__text">
          ⚠️ You're running the {{serverInfo.environment}} command.
        </p>
    </div>
  {%- endif %}
</footer>

<code class="kh-u-show-for-print-only small">Printed direct from AllAboutKen.com</code>
